<title>FRANCE: MOTOR RACING-LEADING PRACTICE TIMES AT FRENCH GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-LEADING PRACTICE TIMES AT FRENCH GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>MAGNY-COURS, France 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading times after</p>
<p>opening practice on Friday for Sunday's French Grand Prix motor</p>
<p>race:</p>
<p>1. Michael Schumacher (Germany) Ferrari one minute and 18.339</p>
<p>seconds (average speed 195.305 kph)</p>
<p>2. Giancarlo Fisichella (Italy) Jordan 1:19.838</p>
<p>3. Mika Hakkinen (Finland) McLaren 1:20.014</p>
<p>4. Ralf Schumacher (Germany) Jordan 1;20.020</p>
<p>5. Jacques Villeneuve (Canada) Williams 1:20.225</p>
<p>6. Heinz-Harald Frentzen (Germany) Williams 1:20.469</p>
<p>7. Jos Verstappen (Netherlands) Tyrrell 1:21.512</p>
<p>8. Jean Alesi (France) Benetton 1:21.742</p>
<p>9. Johnny Herbert (Britain) Sauber 1:22.206</p>
<p>10. Rubens Barrichello (Brazil) Stewart 1:23.232</p>
<p>11. Ukyo Katayama (Japan) Minardi 1:23.469</p>
<p>12. Shinji Nakano (Japan) Prost 1:23.839</p>
